Spec: Project/Modules

Purpose:
  Declare each domain module: what it owns, its public surface, and its
  direct dependencies â€” schema only. Concrete module declarations (e.g.
  payment, course, user) are added once those domains are rebuilt.

Rules:
  A module MUST declare what it owns.
  A module MUST declare its public API surface.
  A module MUST explicitly declare its dependencies (`deps`).
  A module MUST NOT depend on any module not listed in its declared deps
  (undeclared dependency = architecture violation, bax architecture.sdd).
  A module MAY declare `files` (owned source paths) and `entry` (its
   primary entry-point file) once real source exists â€” these are routing
   pointers only, not a second source of truth (see map.sdd -> CodeReference
   -> SourceOfTruth: it is the source for project organization, but runtime
   behavior is still source code itself).
  A module MAY declare `tests` (owned test paths) using the same
  routing-only rule.

Note:
  This file is a SCHEMA â€” concrete module declarations are generated per
  project from templates/_sdd/modules/. This file does not contain
  concrete project data.


State: +

